1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,679
This is the Quest Log on Helm's handheld,

2
00:00:03,129 --> 00:00:08,614
and under Close Inspection's order there's a face: Harbormaster Quill of DS 1.

3
00:00:09,514 --> 00:00:11,809
By the end of today, she's one of yours.

4
00:00:13,609 --> 00:00:15,117
Your map has sides now,

5
00:00:15,567 --> 00:00:16,761
but there's nobody on them.

6
00:00:17,661 --> 00:00:19,335
Today we fix that.

7
00:00:20,235 --> 00:00:21,852
We're going to write three people,

8
00:00:22,302 --> 00:00:24,066
and give each of them a face.

9
00:00:25,866 --> 00:00:27,724
It's one new section in your fact sheet,

10
00:00:28,174 --> 00:00:30,576
and you won't touch the story file at all.

11
00:00:31,776 --> 00:00:34,708
First, one line of the story file, just to read.

12
00:00:35,608 --> 00:00:38,462
In Lecture 11 this line was marked for Class 2.

13
00:00:39,362 --> 00:00:43,518
It makes a person from every record of a section called characters,

14
00:00:43,968 --> 00:00:45,908
so that's the key my section needs.

15
00:00:47,707 --> 00:00:52,878
Now the section itself is two hashes, the word Characters, and that key.

16
00:00:53,778 --> 00:00:56,026
Then the person, with three hashes,

17
00:00:56,476 --> 00:00:59,559
her name, and her key in round brackets.

18
00:01:00,459 --> 00:01:02,704
Inside the fence there's one line,

19
00:01:03,154 --> 00:01:04,932
Face, and the word female.

20
00:01:05,832 --> 00:01:08,490
And below the fence there's a sentence about her,

21
00:01:08,940 --> 00:01:10,385
which is a note for me.

22
00:01:11,285 --> 00:01:14,341
I save, I run lint, and it's clean.

23
00:01:15,541 --> 00:01:17,656
That word female is called a keyword,

24
00:01:18,106 --> 00:01:20,961
and there are seven of them, all for humans.

25
00:01:21,861 --> 00:01:24,055
But a keyword doesn't choose a face.

26
00:01:24,505 --> 00:01:26,568
It asks the game to roll one.

27
00:01:28,368 --> 00:01:30,624
So every time the game starts,

28
00:01:31,074 --> 00:01:34,098
she gets new eyes, new hair and new clothes.

29
00:01:34,998 --> 00:01:38,351
And about half the time she gets skin that's green or blue.

30
00:01:39,251 --> 00:01:41,652
That's fine for a voice the crew hears once.

31
00:01:42,552 --> 00:01:44,519
But it's wrong for a person with a name,

32
00:01:44,969 --> 00:01:47,829
because your crew should know her when she calls again.

33
00:01:49,029 --> 00:01:51,788
To keep a face, the line has to spell it out,

34
00:01:52,238 --> 00:01:54,305
and I'm not going to type that myself.

35
00:01:55,205 --> 00:01:58,265
I press Control, Shift and P,

36
00:01:58,715 --> 00:02:01,765
which opens a box that runs any tool the editor has.

37
00:02:02,665 --> 00:02:05,257
I type story graph, and press Enter.

38
00:02:07,057 --> 00:02:10,146
Here are my records, drawn as boxes,

39
00:02:10,596 --> 00:02:12,676
with one band for each section.

40
00:02:13,576 --> 00:02:16,397
I right-click Quill's box, and I choose Edit.

41
00:02:17,297 --> 00:02:18,966
This tab is the Inspector,

42
00:02:19,416 --> 00:02:22,328
and it shows her record as a form.

43
00:02:23,228 --> 00:02:26,326
Beside her face there's a button, so I click it,

44
00:02:26,776 --> 00:02:29,531
and from the list I choose a random Terran woman.

45
00:02:31,331 --> 00:02:32,375
Now look at my file.

46
00:02:33,275 --> 00:02:35,199
The keyword is gone,

47
00:02:35,649 --> 00:02:38,954
and in its place there's one long line.

48
00:02:39,854 --> 00:02:43,441
That line is her face, written down.

49
00:02:44,641 --> 00:02:46,081
A roll gets me close,

50
00:02:46,531 --> 00:02:48,670
and the builder gets me the rest of the way.

51
00:02:49,569 --> 00:02:52,252
I click her picture, and the Face Builder opens,

52
00:02:52,702 --> 00:02:55,459
starting from the face she already has.

53
00:02:56,359 --> 00:02:58,302
There's a slider for each feature:

54
00:02:58,752 --> 00:03:01,857
eyes, mouth, hair, clothes and so on.

55
00:03:02,757 --> 00:03:04,932
And a tick box beside some of them

56
00:03:05,382 --> 00:03:07,411
turns that feature off altogether.

57
00:03:09,211 --> 00:03:10,521
So I move the hair,

58
00:03:10,971 --> 00:03:14,057
and her line in my file changes while I drag.

59
00:03:14,957 --> 00:03:16,211
There's nothing to press.

60
00:03:17,111 --> 00:03:20,349
When she looks right, I go back to the file and I save.

61
00:03:21,549 --> 00:03:23,320
The second one goes faster.

62
00:03:24,220 --> 00:03:26,237
I type Chief Ives below her,

63
00:03:26,687 --> 00:03:29,295
with the keyword male, and I save.

64
00:03:30,195 --> 00:03:32,772
The graph has already drawn a box for him.

65
00:03:33,672 --> 00:03:36,788
So it's right-click, Edit, the face button,

66
00:03:37,238 --> 00:03:38,621
and a random Terran man.

67
00:03:39,521 --> 00:03:42,032
If I don't care for him, I roll again.

68
00:03:43,232 --> 00:03:45,484
My third person flies the Breaker Cutter,

69
00:03:45,934 --> 00:03:47,950
and she doesn't have to be one of us.

70
00:03:48,849 --> 00:03:50,345
The game has six peoples,

71
00:03:50,795 --> 00:03:53,016
and only the humans have keywords.

72
00:03:53,916 --> 00:03:56,674
For the other five there's no word to type,

73
00:03:57,124 --> 00:03:59,625
so the editor is the only way in.

74
00:04:01,425 --> 00:04:03,153
I type her record the same way,

75
00:04:03,603 --> 00:04:07,119
and this time, from the list, I choose a random Skaraan.

76
00:04:08,019 --> 00:04:11,995
And in the builder, this box at the top is her race.

77
00:04:13,195 --> 00:04:15,455
You'll copy these lines and move them about,

78
00:04:15,905 --> 00:04:18,140
and they break easily, so here are four rules.

79
00:04:19,040 --> 00:04:22,582
A face string is one line, however long it is.

80
00:04:23,482 --> 00:04:26,780
You keep all of it, down to the last semicolon.

81
00:04:27,680 --> 00:04:29,794
You put no quote marks round it.

82
00:04:30,694 --> 00:04:34,024
And you change it with the builder, never by hand.

83
00:04:35,824 --> 00:04:38,893
Here's what the first rule looks like when it's broken.

84
00:04:39,793 --> 00:04:41,819
I press Enter in the middle,

85
00:04:42,269 --> 00:04:44,635
and lint gives me an error on the second half.

86
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:48,606
That's the only one of the four that lint can see,

87
00:04:49,056 --> 00:04:51,320
so the other three are yours to watch.

88
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:54,487
And now the one that will catch you.

89
00:04:55,387 --> 00:04:57,756
I write Face, woman,

90
00:04:58,206 --> 00:05:00,407
which looks just as good as female,

91
00:05:00,857 --> 00:05:02,649
and lint says clean.

92
00:05:04,449 --> 00:05:06,679
But woman isn't one of the seven words,

93
00:05:07,129 --> 00:05:08,998
so the game doesn't roll anything.

94
00:05:09,898 --> 00:05:12,477
It takes the word itself as her face,

95
00:05:12,927 --> 00:05:14,274
and that's no face at all.

96
00:05:15,174 --> 00:05:18,101
Lint knows where a person's record belongs.

97
00:05:18,551 --> 00:05:20,703
It doesn't read what comes after Face.

98
00:05:21,604 --> 00:05:23,702
So that part you check with your own eyes.

99
00:05:24,902 --> 00:05:28,230
Nobody speaks yet, so the game has almost nothing new to show.

100
00:05:29,130 --> 00:05:30,980
But I can look at my cast right here.

101
00:05:31,880 --> 00:05:33,704
I click inside her record,

102
00:05:34,154 --> 00:05:37,210
I open that box again, and I type preview node.

103
00:05:38,110 --> 00:05:41,805
There's Quill, and she'll look like that in every game from now on.

104
00:05:42,705 --> 00:05:44,744
And there's Ives, and there's Sable.

105
00:05:45,944 --> 00:05:48,482
There is one place the game can show her today,

106
00:05:48,932 --> 00:05:50,675
and it's the Quest Log.

107
00:05:51,575 --> 00:05:53,799
Here's Close Inspection, in the list.

108
00:05:54,699 --> 00:05:58,318
Under its order, before the first paragraph, there's Quill.

109
00:05:59,218 --> 00:06:02,223
Her portrait, with her name and her job beside it.

110
00:06:04,023 --> 00:06:07,051
In Class 1 we learned that a description is a page.

111
00:06:07,501 --> 00:06:10,011
A page can hold a face, too.

112
00:06:10,911 --> 00:06:12,363
I don't type her face.

113
00:06:12,813 --> 00:06:14,675
I copy it from her record, all of it,

114
00:06:15,125 --> 00:06:16,944
down to the last semicolon.

115
00:06:17,844 --> 00:06:21,601
Then exclamation mark, empty square brackets,

116
00:06:22,051 --> 00:06:24,785
and face, colon, two slashes.

117
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:28,104
Then I paste, type a closing bracket,

118
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:30,834
and the words that go beside her.

119
00:06:31,734 --> 00:06:33,480
Lint doesn't read that line,

120
00:06:33,930 --> 00:06:38,634
so if you change her face later, change this copy too.

121
00:06:39,834 --> 00:06:43,016
Now it's your turn: add a fourth person of your own,

122
00:06:43,466 --> 00:06:45,249
from a people you haven't used.

123
00:06:46,149 --> 00:06:49,749
Roll a face, and then change two things about it in the builder.

124
00:06:51,549 --> 00:06:54,487
Next time, the harbormaster picks up the microphone.
